From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oleksii Kulinich <entaytion@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 13:38:04 +0300
Subject: Route translation target language through the fork's global setting

The stock translate flow reads/writes its target language through TranslateAlert2
(a per-dialog choice), so entinyGram's own Translator settings target-language
picker had nothing durable to attach to, and a per-dialog choice could silently
clobber the user's global preference.

- InuConfig.TRANSLATE_TARGET_LANGUAGE (added in this same change set) is now
  read first everywhere a target language is resolved; TranslateAlert2 stays the
  fallback for stock behavior when nothing is configured
- a per-dialog language pick no longer overwrites TranslateAlert2's stored value
  once a global target is configured, so it cannot regress back to stock
- isLanguageRestricted gets a respectForceTranslate flag so FORCE_TRANSLATE keeps
  overriding message translation without also forcing the banner on for every chat
- RestrictedLanguagesSelectActivity.isManualChanged() lets a user's Do Not Translate
  edits stick instead of being silently re-derived from system locale
